# Copy this to `.npmrc` in each consuming app repo (scoutpack, etc.).
# It tells npm/pnpm to resolve the @troop10rwc scope from GitHub Packages.
# pnpm reads this same .npmrc format, so no extra config is needed.

@troop10rwc:registry=https://npm.pkg.github.com
//npm.pkg.github.com/:_authToken=${NPM_TOKEN}

# NPM_TOKEN must be a GitHub Personal Access Token with `read:packages`.
#   - Local dev:  put the token in your *user* ~/.npmrc, NOT in the committed file,
#                 or export NPM_TOKEN in your shell.
#   - CI:         add it as a repo secret and expose it as env NPM_TOKEN.
#
# Why a PAT and not the built-in GITHUB_TOKEN? A repo's GITHUB_TOKEN cannot read
# packages published by a *different* repo by default. Either use a PAT, or make
# the package "Internal" visibility (org-wide) and grant this repo access in the
# package settings.
